First game in the tournament.

Since I hadn't ascended a Valkyrie on NAO before, I took this as an
opportunity to do so.

On dlvl1, I found "oR, and I price-ID'd identify on dlvl2.  I planned to
do minetown, but the second level of the mines was dark, and I didn't
have any light source... (I have been playing slashem alot recently,
where I like visiting the mall for light first)

I descended quickly, to sokoban, where I didn't complete the final level
(another "oR there).  Then I decided that I really needed magic
resistance, so I dropped down to the castle.  One notable aspect was the
first altar I found on dlvl14 (the only randomly generated altar, it seems).

I had wear-ID'd =oLev, which allowed me to transverse medusa, and I
ended up meleeing her to death (I don't usually like making myself
permenately invisible, but I had killed a stalker and couldn't wait.)

I arrived at the castle with AC -2, with 120 or so HP.  I navigated the
back corridor (I never actually found /oStriking), and ended had a few
close shaves with death before I managed to clear out the throne room (I
had managed to leave the barracks undisturbed).  The wand was (0:2), and
was used for +3 GDSM (got +0), +3 mitre of holiness (got +3), 2 blessed
?oCharging (got 2), bag of holding, =oTeleControl (I ate a tengu in the
mazes under Medusa and got teleportitus), and wrested for a magic marker
in an attempt to improve my AC.

By this time, I needed 20000XP in order to do the quest, which allowed
Eidolos time to catch up :P.  I did the mines (still with no light
source) and found my first light in Izchak's store (2 wax candles, 5
tallow candles, and a cursed oil lamp).

Minesend was the wine cellar, but I didn't complete it for lack of a
digging tool.

I slipped into the lava on the quest (4 months with hjkl isn't enough),
and lost my +2 iron shoes.  I recovered the orb and the bell with the
help of a /oDeath, and then jumped down to the valley.

I managed to keep the graveyards oblivious to my presence, gave the
priest a bit more for protection, then jumped into gehennom.

It was then that I realised the mistake I had made...

Although I was still ahead of Eidolos, He had chosen a class more suited
to a speedy ascension (magic mapping really speeds up the realworld time
required).

In desperation, I levelported to the VS level (dlvl51), marked the
vibrating square, and continued upwards, using a combination of
randomly teleporting around the place, and using anything that I could
follow (arch liches, master liches, demon lords) to try to locate the
upstairs.  I stumbled on vlad's tower and got the candelabrum, but took
a good 2 hours to map out most of gehennom.  A blessed magic lamp
yielded free action, just in time for orcustown.  By this time, Eidolos
had reached the elemental planes, so I took a break, sent him some
congratulatory mail, and had lunch (3 hours late).

When I got back, I surveyed the situation I had left myself at: AC -10,
a bunch of wands of unknown charges, about 180HP, and a severely stuffed
up memory (mindflayers had taken their toll, as had read-IDing amnesia
[while confused, although it didn't really make a difference]).

Part of me wanted to correct this AC problem, but the only way I could
see of doing that was a pudding farm, and, with exams coming up, I
didn't have the energy.  In the end, I simply said, "screw it", and woke
the wizard.  In the sanctum, the wizard reappeared, then teleported to
the high priest and started having a good little fight.  I figured to
just let them fight, and saw a scroll called VE FORBIDDAYN near the stairs.

My out-of-game knowledge informed me that this was genocide, so,
standing on the upstairs, I read it...

"Sent in some Arch-Liches..."

I uttered some profanities, engraved Elbereth, and waited for the
summoning storm to produce a nice corpse (read cockatrice).  After
dealing with the pandemonium, the wizard still hadn't recovered the
amulet, so I had to venture into the temple.

A well aimed /oDeath blast took out the wizard, the high priest, and my
telepathy.

The mysterious force was very active (another thing I should have taken
into account: Eidolos was at least neutral), and I had to kill the
wizard 10 times in Gehennom (sometimes meleeing him to death: my two
wands were empty at the time).  My HP dropped to as low as 3(202) which
was enough to prompt me to wear "oLS instead of "oR.

Halfway through Gehennom, a malignant aura surrounded me, turning my BoH
to uncursed. My water that I was convinced was holy was actually simply
uncursed, so I decided I needed to do an altar run - taking out the
water from the BoH, dropped the BoH and the amulet, and levelported to
the altar.  I got them blessed with no problem, but while I was waiting
out the timeout in the castle,

It dropped the water back from blessed to uncursed...

Well, that's useful isn't it?

So again, I thought, "screw it".  I recovered my bag and amulet and
continued upwards.

After only a few more close shaves with death, I arrived at medusa,
where a friendly local electric eel blew up a few more of my wands and
rings, including the =oFA.

I cancelled and blessed my final magic lamp... and was rewarded with a
tame djinni.

Well, yet again, "screw it".  This is becoming abit of a patten, isn't it?

Well... I didn't really know anything about the number of charges left
in my wands, I briefly considered going to heaven prematurely, but I
decided to see how far I could go.

Plane of Earth: One of my wands of death had a charge left in it, so
there went the wizard.  My wand of digging ran out of charges, so I had 
some fun #twoweaponing pickaxe and silver saber.

Plane of Air: It seems that a constitution of 20 and half damage allows 
one to remain relatively unscathed, even with an appalling AC.

The Orb of Weight showed me where to go on fire (does it not care about 
intelligence - mine was 13?).

Water was also easy, finding the portal with the orb, then levitating 
over to it before it moved too much.

Finally, I arrived at astral.  Rodney on #nethack indicated that the 
lawful altar was to the left.  After exhausting his various wands, and 
ending world hunger a few times, I found the altar.  I then stripped, 
prayed to lose protection, and stuck on the cursed =oProtection I 
carried around, then offered the amulet.

